  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Roots and fractional exponents are two notations for the same idea. Converting between them turns awkward radical problems into routine exponent arithmetic.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 6.1 — Rational exponent",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\( a^{m/n}=\\sqrt[n]{a^{m}}=\\big(\\sqrt[n]{a}\\big)^{m} \\). The denominator is the root; the numerator is the power.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{a}\\,\\sqrt{b}=\\sqrt{ab} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quotient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{\\sqrt{a}}{\\sqrt{b}}=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{a}{b}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Rationalising",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "multiply by \\( \\dfrac{\\sqrt{b}}{\\sqrt{b}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Evaluate \\( 8^{2/3} \\).</p><p>Take the cube root first, then square:</p>\\[ \\big(\\sqrt[3]{8}\\big)^{2}=2^{2}=4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( \\sqrt{x+3}=5 \\).</p><p>Square both sides: \\( x+3=25 \\):</p>\\[ x=22. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve \\(\\sqrt{3x+1}=x-1\\), checking for extraneous solutions.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Square both sides: \\(3x+1=(x-1)^2=x^2-2x+1\\Rightarrow x^2-5x=0\\Rightarrow x=0\\) or \\(x=5\\). Check \\(x=0\\): \\(1=-1\\) ✗ (extraneous). Check \\(x=5\\): \\(4=4\\) ✓. Solution: \\(x=5\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
